    "message": "Run the dispatch phase in Rust and move the walk's completion\n\nrules/dispatch.rs holds the loop and the steps after it. Social actions and walks have Rust\nfunctions; any other event, and any event one refuses, goes to the Python dispatcher for one event.\nA suppressed social action now says its text from Rust. EventWriter::settle takes the event of the\ndue snapshot and leaves a record a handler wrote for the dispatcher to compare.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
